--TEST--
A `Core\Net\Listener` that a child task returns names no socket in the task that receives it, so using it there throws and the task's own listener at the same position is left alone — `rule:core-classes/net-one-api-three-transports`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Net::listen
// A task returns a listener, and using it outside the task throws an error.
// The program's own listener stays open.

var $own = Core\Net::listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
var $result = Core\Task::all({
    door: fn (): Core\Net\Listener => Core\Net::listen("127.0.0.1", 0),
});
echo "the task returned its listener\n";
try {
    echo $result->door->port(), "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    echo "used outside the task: ", $e->message, "\n";
}
echo "own listener has a port: ", $own->port() > 0 ? "yes" : "no", "\n";
$own->close();
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.net]
listen = true
connect = ["127.0.0.1"]
internal = ["127.0.0.1"]
--EXPECT--
the task returned its listener
used outside the task: Core\Net\Listener::port: this handle is closed
own listener has a port: yes
